  "critical_finding": "BREAKTHROUGH: Concatenation of language-center projected sentence embeddings with TF-IDF Erwaegungen embeddings achieves ratio 0.511 at resolution 3.0 — the first representation where legal purity (0.504) exceeds language purity (0.986). The two methods are complementary: center-projection captures cross-lingual legal concepts while TF-IDF captures fine-grained legal vocabulary. The concatenated 896-dim representation benefits from both strengths simultaneously.",
  "notes": "Cycle combined_20260826 tested 8 representations on 857 BGer decisions with extractable Erwaegungen. Key findings: (1) Concatenation is more than additive — concat achieves ratio 0.511 vs center-projected 0.500 and TF-IDF 0.476 at res 3.0. (2) Center-projection in TF-IDF space is ineffective (ratio 0.389 vs 0.390) because language centers in TF-IDF space are at the origin of disjoint vocabulary regions. (3) Bilinear feature debiasing provides only marginal improvement (ratio 0.378). (4) Concat PCA+TF-IDF underperforms Concat Center+TF-IDF (0.491 vs 0.511 at res 3.0). No scope violations. All artifacts verified. Audit gate PASS."
